      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "While Self-Rubrics tailors complex instructions based on instruction metadata, not all instructions are equally effective for instruction tuning, regardless of their complexity (Chen et al., 2023b; Zhou et al., 2023a). Intuitively, exposing the target LLM to instructions it finds challenging can effectively identify its areas for improvement. Therefore, it is crucial to select the most impactful instructions for aligning the target LLM. We therefore introduce Contrastive Filtering, a method to select the instructions that can effectively enhance the target LLM ft. For clarity, we define the space of all natural language sequences as N. We have the strong LLM fs : N →N, the",
